From 185419f8b348587a4ce2b9afef074fcd09ce3048 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:03:16 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] PlaitOS: adapt Slim Recents

Make the imported Slim Recents work in GrapheneOS's Launcher3 on
Android 17, without AICP's framework and library additions:

- Settings: plain Settings.System keys written by the PlaitOS page
  (plait_slim_recents, _gravity, _expanded_mode, _max_apps, _scale,
  _mem_display) instead of AICP's Settings.System constants. Favorites
  are the launcher's own data and move to its shared preferences (the
  launcher can't write Settings.System).
- Icons: from the launcher's icon factory (LauncherIcons), so they have
  the home screen's shape, badges and themed icons, instead of the old
  copy of the icon normalizer and AICP's icon pack support.
- Thumbnails: ActivityManagerWrapper.getTaskThumbnail (Android 17 moved
  task snapshots behind ITaskSnapshotManager).
- Screen pinning: SystemUiProxy.startScreenPinning instead of AICP's
  IStatusBarService.showScreenPinningRequest; lock task and keyguard
  checks with public APIs.
- Tasks: RECENT_IGNORE_UNAVAILABLE instead of AICP's SLIM_RECENTS flag
  (which no longer changes anything in AICP's framework either).
- Package updates and removals now refresh the cached icons (and drop
  the favorite of a removed app); SystemUI used to call this.
- The panel is created the first time Slim Recents is used, and alt-tab
  goes through the toggle so the tasks are loaded first.
- Removed: the app sidebar, icon packs, the media/album art hooks
  (SystemUI fed them, nothing does now), the per-color and corner
  options, the AICP empty-recents artwork and the unused thumbnail cache
  and screen pinning dialog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
